# <ProjectName> — Agent Guide (generated by `atelier init --ai`)

> This file is machine-facing (agents) and human-editable. Edit only when you understand the consequence; regeneration keeps your changes (diff-based).

## Layout

```
src/components/*.atr.ts    # Atelier components (PascalCase, co-located tests/story)
specs/                     # Intent & acceptance — HUMAN-OWNED, read before editing
atelier.config.json        # Semantic tokens + locked components + agent confirm
.atr/snapshots/            # Screenshot baselines (git-managed)
```

## Commands (the only valid surface)

| Command | Use |
|---|---|
| `atelier dev` | dev server + embedded MCP server (127.0.0.1 + token) |
| `atelier check` | hard gate: types + contract + token validation |
| `atelier lint` | soft constraints |
| `atelier test` | unit/component assertions |
| `atelier snapshot [--update]` | visual baseline; diff MUST be reviewed |
| `atelier review` | local acceptance UI (preview/timeline/diff/approve) |
| `atelier build` / `package` | static dist / Tauri exe |

## Working agreement

1. `specs/` is the intent + acceptance authority; agent may propose updates, human decides
2. Locked components (`atelier.config.json → locked`): never edit without explicit human approval
3. One AI turn = one named checkpoint (`store.commit("AI round N")`)
4. Agents: load `atelier` skill for usage; query `/__atelier/registry` for component/token reality
5. Errors carry `fix` — act on it; never silence an error
6. Changes outside `.atr.ts` (config/deps/locked): stop and ask human

> See `skills/` (SKILL.md) for full usage; `llms.txt` for API reference.
